hadiths[42]{hadithnumber,text}:
"999","a .. The Prophett p- qr,4r, 6-ri concluded contract with the peopleof Khaibartof utilize the land on the conditon that ha the produce of fruits vegetation would be thei share. The Prophett .r,, ,r-r, ,r- usod tof give his wives one hundred Wasq each, eighty Wasq of dates and twenty Wasq of barley (When 'IJmare became the Caliph) h gave the wives of the Prophett .+!..r s p-, the option of eithhaving the land and watas thei share carrying of the previous practice. Some of them choose the land and some choose th Wasq, and 'Aisha L..i,4r choose th land"
"1000","`Umar expelled the Jews and the Christians from Hijaz. When Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had conquered Khaibar, he wanted to expel the Jews from it as its land became the property of Allah, His Apostle, and the Muslims. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) intended to expel the Jews but they requested him to let them stay there on the condition that they would do the labor and get half of the fruits. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) told them, We will let you stay on thus condition"
"1001","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There is none amongst the Muslims who plants a tree or sows seeds"
"1002","It has been narrated on the authority of Abu Sa'id Khudri that a man came to the Prophet (may peace he upon him) and said:Who is the best of men? He replied: A man who fights in the way of Allah spending his wealth and staking his life. The man then asked: Who is next to him (in excellence)? He said: Next to him is a believer who lives in a mountain gorge worshipping hid Lord and sparing men from his mischief"
"1003","Cnce Allah's Messengd-r..r,.u ,r- heard the loud voices of some oPPonents quarrelling at the door. One of them was appealing tof the othtof deduct his debt and asking him tof be lenient but Z2.Thenooyof At-tUtusdqat the othwas saying, By Allah"
"1004","In the mosque I asked Ibn Abi Hadrad tof pay the debts which he owed D€, and ou voices grew louder. Allah's Messeng&.* or,r- heard that while he was in his house. He came tof us raising the curtain of his room and said, O Ka'b!"" I replied"
"1005","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If a man finds his very things with a bankrupt, he has more right to take them back than anyone else."""
"1006","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Before your time the angels received the soul of a man and asked him, 'Did you do any good deeds (in your life)?' He replied, 'I used to order my employees to grant time to the rich person to pay his debts at his convenience.' So Allah said to the angels; ""Excuse him."" Rabi said that (the dead man said), 'I used to be easy to the rich and grant time to the poor.' Or, in another narration, 'grant time to the well-off and forgive the needy,' or, 'accept from the well-off and forgive the needy.'"
"1007","Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"
"1008","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"1009","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"1010","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, It is not lawful for a lady to fast (Nawafil) without the permission of her husband when he is at home; and she should not allow anyone to enter his house except with his permission; and if she spends of his wealth (on charitable purposes) without being ordered by him"
"1011","`Umar asked the people, Who remembers the narration of the Prophet (ﷺ) about the affliction?"" Hudhaifa said"
"1012","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, If someone keeps a dog neither for guarding livestock"
"1013","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Whoever keeps a dog"
"1014","A'isha (Allah be pleased with her), wife of Allah's Apostle (ﷺ), heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If your people, had not been recent converts to Islam, I would have spent the treasure of the Ka'ba in the way of Allah and would have constructed its door just on the level of the ground and would have encompassed in it the space of Hijr"
"1015","that he was asked about the wages of the one who cups others. He said, 'Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was cupped by `Abd Taiba, to whom he gave two Sa of food and interceded for him with his masters who consequently reduced what they used to charge him daily. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) s said, ""The best medicines you may treat yourselves with are cupping and sea incense.' He added, ""You should not torture your children by treating tonsillitis by pressing the tonsils or the palate with the finger, but use incense."""
"1016","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""Amongst the trees, there is a tree, the leaves of which do not fall and is like a Muslim. Tell me the name of that tree."" Everybody started thinking about the trees of the desert areas. And I thought of the date-palm tree but felt shy to answer the others then asked, ""What is that tree, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) ?"" He replied, ""It is the date-palm tree."""
"1017","When the Verses of Sfirat Al-Baqarah abo the Ribd'l' (usury) were revealed, the Prophett p- -.r, .rr- w€rt tof the mosque and recited them in front of the people and then banned the trade of alcoholic drinks. Prohibition of the trade (sale) of alcoholic liquors, dead animals, pigs, and idols. l0l8.Narrated Jdbi bin'Abdulldh ' -r. .r : I heard Allah's Messengu' . l-:,), in the yeare of the conquest of Makka, saying, Allah and His Messengmade illegal the trade of alcoholic liquors"
"1018","That he heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) describing the period of pause of the Divine Inspiration, and in his description he said, ""While I was walking I heard a voice from the sky. I looked up towards the sky, and behold! I saw the same Angel who came to me in the Cave of Hira', sitting on a chair between the sky and the earth. I was so terrified by him that I fell down on the ground. Then I went to my wife and said, 'Wrap me in garments! Wrap me in garments!' They wrapped me, and then Allah revealed: ""O you, (Muhammad) wrapped-up! Arise and warn...and desert the idols."" (74.1-5) Abu Salama said....Rujz means idols."" After that, the Divine Inspiration started coming more frequently and regularly."
"1019","I proceeded till I entered upon `Umar (and while I was sitting there), his gate-keeper Yarfa came to him and said,  `Uthman"
"1020","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"1021","When the mountain of Uhud came in the sight of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) he said. This is a mountain that loves us and is loved by us. O Allah! Abraham made Mecca a sanctuary"
"1022","This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Shu'ba through a different chain of transmitters"
"1023","i,.u' ,-r- forbade the selling of gold fgold and silvfsilve except if they are equivalent in weight (and from hand tof hand), and allowed us tof sell gold fsilvand vice versa as we wished. 22. Thre Book of Al-Musflqat Sale of food grains like flike"""
"1024","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) appointed somebody as a governor of Khaibar. That governor brought to him an excellent kind of dates (from Khaibar). The Prophet (ﷺ) asked, Are all the dates of Khaibar like this?"" He replied"
"1025","Once Bilal brought Barni (i.e. a kind of dates) to the Prophet (ﷺ) and the Prophet (ﷺ) asked him, From where have you brought these?"" Bilal replied"
"1026","We used to be given mixed dates (from the booty) and used to sell (barter) two Sas of those dates) for one Sa (of good dates). The Prophet (ﷺ) said (to us), No (bartering of) two Sas for one Sa nor two Dirhams for one Dirham is permissible"""
"1027","I heard Ab Sa'id Al-Khudri r:e d u saying, The selling of a Dind fa Dindr"
"1028","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Who ever is pleased that he be granted more wealth and that his lease of life be pro longed"
"1029","While I was riding a (slow and) tired camel the Prophett d-r..r, orr.- passed by and beat it and prayed fAllah's Blessings fit' The camel became sof fast as it had nevbeen before. The Prophett '.r orr- &- then said"
"1030","Jabir b. Abdullah (Allah be pleased with them) reported:Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) visited the orchard of Umm Ma'sud and said: Umm Ma'bad. he who has planted this tree, is he a Muslim or a non-Muslim? She said: Of course, he is a Muslim, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: No Muslim who plants (trees) and from their fruits the human beings or the beasts or birds eat, but that would be taken as an act of charity on the Day of Resurrection"
"1031","A hadith like this has been narrated on the authority of Juraij with the same chain of transmitters"
"1032","A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) demanding his debts and behaved rudely. The companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) intended to harm him, but Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said (to them), Leave him"
"1033","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Faith (Belief) consists of more than sixty branches (i.e. parts). And Haya (This term ""Haya"" covers a large number of concepts which are to be taken together; amongst them are self respect, modesty, bashfulness, and scruple, etc.) is a part of faith."""
"1034","The Prophet (ﷺ) came to Medina and the people used to pay in advance the price of dates to be delivered within two or three years. He said (to them), Whoever pays in advance the price of a thing to be delivered later should pay it for a specified measure at specified weight for a specified period."""""
"1035","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"
"1036","u : Allah's Messengd-r.+.l 3- gave the verdict of pre-emption (Shuf'a) fevery undivided joint thing (property). But if the limits are defined (demarcated) the ways and streets are fixed, then there is nof pre-emption. Tof lix a wooden peg in the wall of one's neighbour"
"1037","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"1038","Hudhaifa b. Usaid reported:Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) was in an apartment and we were beneath that, that he peeped in and said to us: What are you discussing about? We said: (We are discussing about the Last) Hour. Thereupon he said: The Last Hour would not come until the ten signs appear: land-sliding in the east, and land-sliding in the west, and land-sliding in the peninsula of Arabia, the smoke, the Dajjal, the beast of the earth, Gog and Magog, the rising of the sun from the west and the fire which would emit from the lower part of 'Adan. Shu'ba said that 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Rufai' reported on the authority of Abu Tufail who reported on the authority of Abu Sariha a hadith like this that Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) did not make a mention of (the tenth sign) but he said that out of the ten one was the descent of Jesus, son of Mary (peace be upon him), and in another version it is the blowing of the violent gale which would drive the people to the ocean"
"1039","That there was a dispute between him and some people (about a piece of land). When he told `Aisha about it, she said, ""O Abu Salama! Avoid taking the land unjustly, for the Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'Whoever usurps even one span of the land of somebody, his neck will be encircled with it down the seven earths."""
"1040","4,urr-r- judged that seven cubits should be left as a public way when there was a dispute about the land. 23.TheBoolof Al-Fara'ia 23. THE BOOK OB AL.FARA'ID (The laws of inheritance) Give the Fard'id (shares of inheritance prescribed in the Qur'An) tof those whof are entitled tof receive it then whatevremains should be given tof the closest male relative of the deceased. . Nanated Ibn 'Abbis ur:"" ut I The Prophett p-r.+r"
